opentitan: fixes for slang (svcheck corpora opentitan-*)

What VCS accepts in OpenTitan's DV and slang 11 rejects as an error, in the IPs
tests/corpora/corpora.yaml compiles. Each change keeps the bench's meaning.

- hmac_scoreboard: the streaming concatenation reverses the bytes of a 32-bit
  value: a 64-bit uvm_reg_data_t streamed into a 32-bit target is an error (11.4.14).
- hmac_common_vseq, pattgen_{cnt_rollover,perf}_vseq: an override of a protected
  virtual method is protected too; slang refuses one that widens its access.

diff --git a/hw/ip/hmac/dv/env/hmac_scoreboard.sv b/hw/ip/hmac/dv/env/hmac_scoreboard.sv
index efa2ee9..aacdd96 100644
--- a/hw/ip/hmac/dv/env/hmac_scoreboard.sv
+++ b/hw/ip/hmac/dv/env/hmac_scoreboard.sv
@@ -351,7 +351,7 @@ task hmac_scoreboard::process_tl_access(tl_seq_item item, tl_channels_e channel,
           // `exp_digest` with the prediction.
           int digest_idx = get_digest_index(csr_name);
           if (`gmv(ral.cfg.digest_swap)) begin
-            exp_digest[digest_idx] = {<<8{`gmv(csr)}};
+            exp_digest[digest_idx] = {<<8{32'(`gmv(csr))}};
           end else begin
             exp_digest[digest_idx] = `gmv(csr);
           end
